? Why is financial data especially suitable for data mining?
+ It is usually fairly complete, reliable and of high quality
- It is always small enough to fit in a spreadsheet
- It has no structure, so any algorithm can be used
- It is rarely stored digitally, so it is easy to collect
= That supports systematic analysis.

? Which technique helps identify the critical factors behind loan payment performance?
+ Attribute selection and attribute relevance ranking
- Sequence alignment of the customers' payment records
- Grid-based clustering of the customers
- Market basket analysis of loan products
= It also removes irrelevant factors.

? To detect money laundering, it is essential to:
+ Integrate data from several databases, then look for unusual patterns
- Analyse one bank's transactions on their own, without other sources
- Delete old transaction histories to protect privacy
- Look only at each account's average monthly balance
= For example, large cash flows at certain periods by certain customer groups.

? Why is retail data growing so quickly?
+ The ease and popularity of e-commerce
- Shops are closing their tills
- Retailers stopped collecting data
- Only cash sales are recorded
= E-commerce adds large volumes of transaction and interaction data; firms may combine online and physical channels.

? How can a retailer analyse the effectiveness of a sales campaign?
+ Compare sales of the promoted items during vs before and after
- Count how many staff worked during the campaign
- Look only at the total sales in last year's tax return
- Measure how full the warehouse was after the campaign
= This is a use of multidimensional analysis.

? Which is a typical dimension of telecommunication data?
+ Calling time, duration, and caller and callee location
- Gene sequence, protein structure and mutation rate
- Product price, shelf position and promotion type
- Loan amount, interest rate and repayment history
= Multidimensional analysis compares traffic, workload, resource usage and profit.

? Which is one of the three fraud tasks in telecommunications?
+ Detecting attempts to gain fraudulent entry to customer accounts
- Lowering call prices for the most loyal long-term customers
- Planning where to build new towers for coverage
- Printing up-to-date phone books for each region
= The others: find fraudulent users and atypical usage; discover unusual patterns.

? Periodic calls from badly programmed automatic dial-out equipment (like fax machines) are an example of:
+ An unusual pattern that needs special attention
- A normal busy-hour pattern of call traffic
- A biological sequence alignment problem
- A successful retail sales campaign
= Others include busy-hour frustrated call attempts and route congestion.

? Finding usage patterns for services by customer group, month and time of day uses:
+ Multidimensional association and sequential pattern analysis
- k-medoids clustering of the call detail records by duration
- Money laundering detection across banks
- Gaussian naive Bayes on call durations
= It's used to promote telecom services.

? Biological data mining is an essential part of which field?
+ Bioinformatics
- Telemarketing
- Accounting
- Logistics
= It covers genomics and proteomics.

? BLAST and FASTA are tools for:
+ Aligning and comparing DNA or protein sequences
- Clustering supermarket customers by basket
- Detecting fraud in telecom call records
- Building data warehouses for banks
= They must allow gaps and mismatches.

? Why must biological sequence analysis allow gaps and mismatches?
+ To handle insertions, deletions and mutations
- To make the sequence data smaller to store
- Because the order of DNA bases does not matter
- To speed up the comparison over the network
= That's how it differs from ordinary sequential pattern mining.

? Genomic and proteomic data sets need semantic integration mainly because they are:
+ Produced by different labs and methods, so heterogeneous
- Always identical, so they can simply be merged
- Too small to analyse unless they are all combined into one
- Stored only on paper in different countries
= Linking research literature to biological entities also matters.
